## 2. G3 execution protocol (gate = note_17 §2 G3, verbatim; four sub-gates, Profiler + Validator both sign)

### 2.0 Setup invariants

- Graph under test: the **dynamo** ONNX only. OV `2026.2.1`, GPU.0, **f32**. (f16 may be probed afterward as a data point — it is not a gate and the monolith f16 MatMul failure predicts nothing good.)
- Noise inputs (`sine_noise [1,57600,9]`, `phase_rand [1,9]`) generated CPU-side per request; their generation cost is **included** in end-to-end RTF.
- Every timing table names its methodology per WORKFLOW.md: cold vs steady, warmup handling, and the RTF denominator — which is the **real-region** audio duration (T_native×600/24000 s), with the padded-bucket duration also reported for honesty.

### 2.1 Offload proof (gate item 1)

`EXECUTION_DEVICES == ['GPU.0']` printed; GPU kernels in a profile capture; `intel_gpu_top` RCS busy during sustained infer. Provider names are not proof (house rule).

**Contingency A (from note_17, still live):** if OV GPU compile fails with the 3D `linear_onnx` Interpolate class, port `patch_kokoro_resize.py` logic to the decoder ONNX, log it, continue.
**Contingency B (new — dynamo graph shape):** if OV fails on dynamo-specific op patterns (opset 18 lowerings the plugin dislikes), **stop and report the exact op/error**. Do not fall back to the legacy graph — it fails parity. Options at that point (Fable turn): targeted graph rewrite of the offending pattern, or dynamo re-export at opset 17. Parity must be re-proven for whatever graph OV actually consumes.

### 2.2 No per-utterance JIT (gate item 2 — the falsifiable core)

1. Cold: first compile+infer at T=96, timed and reported separately. Prediction: compile 5–30 s once per process without cache; this is expected and not a failure.
2. Warm run: **≥10 novel texts** (all T_native ≤ 96, varied lengths 60–95, edge-padded), each with fresh noise draws. **PASS:** zero multi-second first-infers; every novel-text infer within 10% of the warm mean. **KILL:** any 17–25s-class JIT event on a novel text at the warmed bucket.
3. Include at least 2 repeats of one text to show run-to-run warm stability in the same table.

### 2.3 Restart persistence (gate item 3)

With `CACHE_DIR` set: run 2.2, record cache dir listing (file count + total bytes). Kill process. Restart, recompile T=96: **PASS** compile ≤ 2 s and first infer lands warm (within the 2.2 warm envelope). Report dir listing after, and the compile-time delta cold-vs-cached in one row.

### 2.4 Realtime (gate item 4)

End-to-end warm steady-state on real text: CPU frontend (incl. noise gen) → edge pad → OV-GPU decoder → real-region trim. **PASS:** RTF ≤ 1.0 by the real-region denominator. Prediction: ≤ 0.9 — the decoder is the audio-rate 65% of compute and whole-graph warm already achieved 0.9; a static compile should do no worse and plausibly better. Report cold separately; never average it in (note_11 rule).

### 2.5 Quality tie-off

One parity check of OV-GPU output vs ORT-CPU on identical inputs+noise (aligned corr; expect the known small GPU fidelity delta class from the monolith work), plus a ≥3-utterance ear set for Nexus by filename — G3's claims are performance claims, but no performance claim ships without ears attached (house rule).

